abstract: >-
  A minimal realization of the Zero Tier Execution Substrate (ZTES) published in Systems 14 (2026)
  547, from which it takes its name, and the executable supplement to "A Calculus of Execution for
  Interacting Binary Relations" and to "Observable, Governable, Cooperative: Execution Analytics and
  Adaptive Heuristic Agents in the OEE Calculus" (in preparation). Its fixed admission procedure Z0, which with the architecture
  S1 forms the zero-tier execution substrate, applies Axiom 0 to
  systems of abstractions given as JSON specifications, with nine worked examples, eight defective
  mechanisms for the essential conditions of S1, and replay under R2.
keywords: [execution calculus, binary relations, append-only record, replay, admission]
